    "154": "\\emph{Rough comparisons.} For $0<\\tau<1/2$, the upper bound below",
    "577": "There are at most $(k+1)e^{kh(\\tau)}$ subsets with $r\\le\\tau k$, and",
    "578": "$\\log\\binom{k}{r}\\le kh(\\tau)$.  Cauchy--Schwarz for",
    "579": "$A_{j,g}^{-1/2}\\sum_Bu_B$, followed by",
    "580": "\\eqref{comparator:component-inverse}, proves",
    "581": "\\begin{equation}",
    "582": " \\Pi A_{j,g}^{-1}\\Pi",
    "583": "       \\le\\exp\\{-kaL_{j,g}+o(k)\\}\\Pi,",
    "584": " \\quad",
    "585": " L_{j,g}=2S'+(1-\\tau)g_{j,g}^{\\mathrm{pre}}",
    "586": "          -C\\left(\\tau\\log d_*+\\frac{h(\\tau)}a+a\\mathcal B\\right).",
    "587": " \\label{comparator:inverse-compression}",
    "588": "\\end{equation}",
    "589": "In the rough version set $g^{\\mathrm{pre}}=0$ and omit $a\\mathcal B$.",
    "590": "The factor counting subsets is precisely the source of $h(\\tau)/a$."
  }
}
